{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6109220","formula":"C₂₂H₂₅NO","hill":"C22H25NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":22.0,"H":25.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"JWH-251"},"descriptions":{"en":"JWH-251 (1-pentyl-3-(2-methylphenylacetyl)indole) is a synthetic cannabinoid from the phenylacetylindole family, which acts as a cannabinoid agonist with about five times selectivity for CB1 with a Ki of 29 nM and 146 nM at CB2. Similar to the related 2'-methoxy compound JWH-250, the 2'-chloro compound JWH-203, and the 2'-bromo compound JWH-249, JWH-251 has a phenylacetyl group in place of the naphthoyl ring used in most aminoalkylindole cannabinoid compounds. In the United States, all CB1 receptor agonists of the 3-phenylacetylindole class such as JWH-251 are Schedule I Controlled Substances."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":11616723,"mass":319.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCN1C=C(C2=CC=CC=C21)C(=O)CC3=CC=CC=C3C","inchikey":"YBIPNGRKUAVSBG-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(2-methylphenyl)-1-(1-pentylindol-3-yl)ethanone","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11616723","atoms":49,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.182,"y":-1.385,"z":-0.31,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.095,"y":-0.172,"z":0.68,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.282,"y":0.57,"z":1.089,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.966,"y":1.324,"z":-0.054,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.087,"y":-1.471,"z":0.245,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.758,"y":-1.79,"z":-0.043,"el":"C"},{"x":0.02,"y":-0.633,"z":0.238,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.835,"y":0.349,"z":0.682,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.205,"y":2.103,"z":0.397,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.807,"y":2.903,"z":-0.758,"el":"C"},{"x":1.439,"y":-0.464,"z":0.101,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.136,"y":-2.383,"z":0.083,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.459,"y":-3.084,"z":-0.516,"el":"C"},{"x":2.1,"y":0.884,"z":0.461,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.815,"y":-3.66,"z":-0.388,"el":"C"},{"x":3.601,"y":0.909,"z":0.31,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.4